  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Translate the lesson into explicit state and permissive logic: Charging is enabled only for an occupied, authorized, ready bay.",
      "Inputs are simulator feedback (bay_occupied, customer_authorized, charger_ready); PLC logic owns charge_enable, energy_session_active.",
      "Test the initial state, the valid condition, and at least one missing permissive.",
      "Illustrative offline fixture: 6 kW shared allocation budget; .001 kWh per meter pulse. PLC owns bay grants, allocated_kw and energy_count/energy_kwh. No charging protocol, calibration or electrical approval. Explicit review reference is generated by --audit-ev-layout; native runtime verification remains pending.",
      "Unplug before vehicle removal. Connector fixture changes require charge_enable false and allocation zero. Energy integrates accepted ticks only; Stop retains meter energy and fractional pulse state, while Reset clears them.",
      "The review reference grants 6 kW to one eligible bay or 3 kW each to two. PLC acknowledges the cumulative meter event ledger so Stop between a pulse and the next scan cannot lose or double-count it. The installed readout shows PLC accumulated kWh; standalone meter assets remain static."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Require the documented inputs: bay_occupied, customer_authorized, charger_ready.",
        "Command the documented outputs: charge_enable, energy_session_active.",
        "Remove PLC commands when the permissive is lost."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Charging is enabled only for an occupied, authorized, ready bay."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "EV/charger bay",
      "connector latch",
      "energy meter",
      "pulse-output meter",
      "authorization reader"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "A shared controller allocates charging permission and accumulates energy pulse events for occupied bays.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Apply the requested input condition.",
        "Verify only the documented PLC outputs respond."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Removing the permissive removes PLC-owned commands.",
        "Reset returns the module to its initial state."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing or stale input must fail safe and remain diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "Charging is enabled only for an occupied, authorized, ready bay."
      ]
    },
    "sequenceNumber": 58,
